('rp-pte-expansion-fill-in-blanks-rw-4', 'pte-2026-01', 'Shared research equipment', '[{"label": "A", "text": "Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user. A committee initially proposed charging departments for every minute of access. Technicians warned that this might discourage necessary cleaning and calibration between sessions. The committee instead introduced protected maintenance periods and required users to estimate preparation time separately from measurement time. It also appointed a coordinator to resolve conflicts. Utilisation fell slightly because the timetable now included maintenance, yet fewer experiments had to be repeated. The departments concluded that keeping the machine continuously occupied was a poor substitute for producing reliable results. Sharing equipment required investment in coordination as well as agreement over purchase costs."}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 0, 'medium', 'Community and research', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice'], TRUE, 'custom'),
('rp-pte-expansion-fill-in-blanks-r-4', 'pte-2026-01', 'Shared research equipment', '[{"label": "A", "text": "Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user. A committee initially proposed charging departments for every minute of access. Technicians warned that this might discourage necessary cleaning and calibration between sessions. The committee instead introduced protected maintenance periods and required users to estimate preparation time separately from measurement time. It also appointed a coordinator to resolve conflicts. Utilisation fell slightly because the timetable now included maintenance, yet fewer experiments had to be repeated. The departments concluded that keeping the machine continuously occupied was a poor substitute for producing reliable results. Sharing equipment required investment in coordination as well as agreement over purchase costs."}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 0, 'medium', 'Community and research', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice'], TRUE, 'custom'),
