('pte-expansion-001', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-rw', 'Reading & Writing: Fill in the Blanks', 'Repair cafes', 'Select the best word for each blank.', 180, 0, 1, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'In context, the missing words are purpose, participate, recurring.', 'rp-pte-expansion-fill-in-blanks-rw-1', 'g-pte-expansion-fill-in-blanks-rw-1', 'A repair cafe brings volunteers and residents together to fix household objects. Its [[b1]] is not simply to save the price of a replacement. By explaining each step, volunteers help owners understand why an object failed and how to maintain it. Some visitors arrive expecting a free repair service, however, and feel disappointed when they must [[b2]]. Organisers therefore describe the learning element clearly before accepting bookings. They also record items that cannot be repaired. These records can reveal [[b3]] design problems, although they cannot establish how common a fault is across all products sold. A cafe sees only the objects that people choose to bring. Manufacturers could still use this limited evidence to identify components worth investigating. The strongest argument for a cafe is consequently educational rather than statistical: a successful visit can change the way someone thinks about ownership, even when the object itself remains broken.', '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["purpose", "profit", "surface", "distance"], "correctAnswer": "purpose"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["disappear", "compete", "purchase", "participate"], "correctAnswer": "participate"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["imaginary", "unrelated", "recurring", "temporary"], "correctAnswer": "recurring"}]'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-002', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'reading', 'fill-in-blanks-r', 'Reading: Fill in the Blanks', 'Repair cafes', 'Select the best word for each blank.', 180, 0, 1, 3, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'In context, the missing words are purpose, participate, recurring.', 'rp-pte-expansion-fill-in-blanks-r-1', 'g-pte-expansion-fill-in-blanks-r-1', 'A repair cafe brings volunteers and residents together to fix household objects. Its [[b1]] is not simply to save the price of a replacement. By explaining each step, volunteers help owners understand why an object failed and how to maintain it. Some visitors arrive expecting a free repair service, however, and feel disappointed when they must [[b2]]. Organisers therefore describe the learning element clearly before accepting bookings. They also record items that cannot be repaired. These records can reveal [[b3]] design problems, although they cannot establish how common a fault is across all products sold. A cafe sees only the objects that people choose to bring. Manufacturers could still use this limited evidence to identify components worth investigating. The strongest argument for a cafe is consequently educational rather than statistical: a successful visit can change the way someone thinks about ownership, even when the object itself remains broken.', '[{"id": "b1", "options": ["compete", "disappear", "distance", "imaginary", "participate", "profit", "purchase", "purpose", "recurring", "surface", "temporary", "unrelated"], "correctAnswer": "purpose"}, {"id": "b2", "options": ["compete", "disappear", "distance", "imaginary", "participate", "profit", "purchase", "purpose", "recurring", "surface", "temporary", "unrelated"], "correctAnswer": "participate"}, {"id": "b3", "options": ["compete", "disappear", "distance", "imaginary", "participate", "profit", "purchase", "purpose", "recurring", "surface", "temporary", "unrelated"], "correctAnswer": "recurring"}]'::jsonb, NULL,