ngs. They also record items that cannot be repaired. These records can reveal recurring design problems, although they cannot establish how common a fault is across all products sold. A cafe sees only the objects that people choose to bring. Manufacturers could still use this limited evidence to identify components worth investigating. The strongest argument for a cafe is consequently educational rather than statistical: a successful visit can change the way someone thinks about ownership, even when the object itself remains broken.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
