fferent results. Nevertheless, the interviews did not prove that demand would eventually cover operating costs. The researchers recommended comparing the service with alternatives, including a shared taxi scheme. They proposed recording who benefited, how reliably vehicles arrived and the cost per completed journey. The council postponed its final decision until this broader evidence was available.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
