"w135", "text": "costs."}]'::jsonb, '["w20", "w61", "w121"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user. A committee initially proposed charging departments for every minute of access. Technicians warned that this might discourage necessary cleaning and calibration between sessions. The committee instead introduced protected maintenance periods and required users to estimate preparation time separately from measurement time. It also appointed a coordinator to resolve conflicts. Utilisation fell slightly because the timetable now included maintenance, yet fewer experiments had to be repeated. The departments concluded that keeping the machine continuously occupied was a poor substitute for producing reliable results. Sharing equipment required investment in coordination as well as agreement over purchase costs.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-055', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'pte-select-missing-word', 'Select Missing Word', 'Shared research equipment', 'The final word is omitted from this practice recording. Select the word that completes the speaker''s meaning.', 120, 0, 0, 1, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'The conclusion ends with coordination. This practice uses a pause, not a recorded beep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "decoration"}, {"id": "B", "text": "coordination"}, {"id": "C", "text": "permission"}, {"id": "D", "text": "competition"}]'::jsonb, '["B"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user. A committee initially proposed charging departments for every minute of access. Technicians warned that this might discourage necessary cleaning and calibration between sessions. The committee instead introduced protected maintenance periods and required users to estimate preparation time separately from measurement time. It also appointed a coordinator to resolve conflicts. Utilisation fell slightly because the timetable now included maintenance, yet fewer experiments had to be repeated. The departments concluded that keeping the machine continuously occupied was a poor substitute for producing reliable results. Sharing equipment required investment in coordination as well as agreement over purchase costs. Sharing a machine successfully depends not only on access but also on ...', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-056', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'write-from-dictation', 'Write from Dictation', 'Shared research equipment', 'Listen to the sentence and type exactly what you hear.', 60, 0, 0, 9, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Reference sentence: Please include preparation time when booking the shared equipment.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["Please include preparation time when booking the shared equipment."]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Please include preparation time when booking the shared equipment.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-057', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'summarize-spoken-text', 'Summarize Spoken Text', 'Shared research equipment', 'Listen to the talk and summarise its main points in 50-70 words. You have 10 minutes. Practice feedback is an approximate content/form check, not an official PTE score.', 600, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Departments sharing an imaging instrument found that protected maintenance and coordinated scheduling improved reliability despite slightly lower utilisation, demonstrating that successful sharing involves more than reducing purchase costs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["equipment", "maintenance", "coordination", "reliable", "costs"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user. A committee initially proposed charging departments for every minute of access. Technicians warned that this might discourage necessary cleaning and calibration between sessions. The committee instead introduced protected maintenance periods and required users to estimate preparation time separately from measurement time. It also appointed a coordinator to resolve conflicts. Utilisation fell slightly because the timetable now included maintenance, yet fewer experiments had to be repeated. The departments concluded that keeping the machine continuously occupied was a poor substitute for producing reliable results. Sharing equipment required investment in coordination as well as agreement over purchase costs. A utilisation figure can look impressive while concealing avoidable errors. If a machine runs all day but produces measurements that must be repeated, the apparent efficiency is misleading. Maintenance may reduce available booking hours while increasing useful output. The coordinator therefore tracked repeat experiments and reasons for delays alongside total use. Researchers also received training in estimating their needs. This did not remove every conflict, especially before important deadlines, but it made the basis for allocating time clearer. Departments considering shared facilities could begin by discussing these practical responsibilities rather than focusing exclusively on the price of the instrument.', 'Departments sharing an imaging instrument found that protected maintenance and coordinated scheduling improved reliability despite slightly lower utilisation, demonstrating that successful sharing involves more than reducing purchase costs. The speaker illustrates why a simple measure can be misleading and argues that decisions should reflect the purpose of the activity as well as the limitations of the available evidence.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-058', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcma', 'MCQ Multiple Answer', 'Community rainfall records', 'Listen and select all supported statements.', 150, 0, 0, 2, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Some observers moved their measuring containers."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Official weather stations had operated at every diary location."}, {"id": "C", "text": "Images allowed users to check uncertain handwriting."}, {"id": "D", "text": "The group discarded all records with inconsistent methods."}]'::jsonb, '["A", "C"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-059', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'pte-listening-mcsa', 'MCQ Single Answer', 'Community rainfall records', 'What is the main point of the recording?', 150, 0, 0, 1, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Historical observations become more useful when their limitations are documented."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Every missing diary entry was converted to zero rainfall."}, {"id": "C", "text": "All residents had used identical measuring equipment."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Digitisation removed every uncertainty in the original observations."}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-060', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'pte-highlight-correct-summary', 'Highlight Correct Summary', 'Community rainfall records', 'Listen and select the best summary.', 150, 0, 0, 1, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days."}, {"id": "B", "text": "Every missing diary entry was converted to zero rainfall."}, {"id": "C", "text": "All residents had used identical measuring equipment."}, {"id": "D", "text": "Digitisation removed every uncertainty in the original observations."}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
