140", "text": "never"}, {"id": "w141", "text": "anticipated."}]'::jsonb, '["w5", "w74", "w125"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-063', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'pte-select-missing-word', 'Select Missing Word', 'Community rainfall records', 'The final word is omitted from this practice recording. Select the word that completes the speaker''s meaning.', 120, 0, 0, 1, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'The conclusion ends with documentation. This practice uses a pause, not a recorded beep.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"id": "A", "text": "documentation"}, {"id": "B", "text": "permission"}, {"id": "C", "text": "competition"}, {"id": "D", "text": "decoration"}]'::jsonb, '["A"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated. For later researchers, the numbers are most useful when accompanied by careful ...', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-064', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'write-from-dictation', 'Write from Dictation', 'Community rainfall records', 'Listen to the sentence and type exactly what you hear.', 60, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Reference sentence: The original diaries remain available in the local history archive.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["The original diaries remain available in the local history archive."]'::jsonb, NULL, 'The original diaries remain available in the local history archive.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-065', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'listening', 'summarize-spoken-text', 'Summarize Spoken Text', 'Community rainfall records', 'Listen to the talk and summarise its main points in 50-70 words. You have 10 minutes. Practice feedback is an approximate content/form check, not an official PTE score.', 600, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '["rainfall", "diaries", "methods", "missing", "documentation"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated. Imagine two neighbouring diaries showing different totals for the same month. One observer may have measured in an open space, while another kept a container beneath a tree. Without contextual notes, a researcher might interpret the difference as a variation in weather. Documentation does not tell us exactly how much rain fell, but it helps us avoid unjustified certainty. The distinction between missing and zero values is equally important. A person may have been away for a week or simply forgotten to write. Preserving that uncertainty is more honest than filling every empty cell with a convenient number.', 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days. The speaker illustrates why a simple measure can be misleading and argues that decisions should reflect the purpose of the activity as well as the limitations of the available evidence.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-066', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'Repair cafes', 'Summarise the passage in ONE sentence of 5-75 words. You have 10 minutes.', 600, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Repair cafes teach owners maintenance skills through participation, while records of failed repairs can suggest design issues but cannot establish their prevalence because visitors bring a self-selected sample of products.', NULL, NULL, 'A repair cafe brings volunteers and residents together to fix household objects. Its purpose is not simply to save the price of a replacement. By explaining each step, volunteers help owners understand why an object failed and how to maintain it. Some visitors arrive expecting a free repair service, however, and feel disappointed when they must participate. Organisers therefore describe the learning element clearly before accepting bookings. They also record items that cannot be repaired. These records can reveal recurring design problems, although they cannot establish how common a fault is across all products sold. A cafe sees only the objects that people choose to bring. Manufacturers could still use this limited evidence to identify components worth investigating. The strongest argument for a cafe is consequently educational rather than statistical: a successful visit can change the way someone thinks about ownership, even when the object itself remains broken. Consider a visitor with a desk lamp. A volunteer may find that a replacement switch is no longer available. The visit has not restored the lamp, but the owner has learned why access to spare parts matters. That knowledge may influence a later purchase. Another visitor may decide to clean an appliance regularly after seeing how dust affected its performance. Neither outcome appears in a count of completed repairs. Organisers should therefore ask what participants learned, as well as whether their objects function again. Enthusiasm should not replace safety: volunteers need clear limits on their work and should refer unsuitable jobs to qualified professionals.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Repair cafes teach owners maintenance skills through participation, while records of failed repairs can suggest design issues but cannot establish their prevalence because visitors bring a self-selected sample of products.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-067', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-read-aloud', 'Read Aloud', 'Repair cafes', 'Prepare for 35 seconds, then read the passage aloud clearly and naturally.', 40, 35, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Read all words accurately; group words into meaningful phrases rather than pausing after each word.', NULL, NULL, 'A repair cafe brings volunteers and residents together to fix household objects. Its purpose is not simply to save the price of a replacement. By explaining each step, volunteers help owners understand why an object failed and how to maintain it.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-068', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-repeat-sentence', 'Repeat Sentence', 'Repair cafes', 'Listen, then repeat the sentence exactly as spoken.', 15, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Preserve the original word sequence and grammatical endings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The workshop accepts bookings through the community centre website.', 'The workshop accepts bookings through the community centre website.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-069', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-answer-short-question', 'Answer Short Questions', 'Repair cafes', 'Listen to the question and answer with one or a few words.', 10, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Expected answer: A volunteer. Equivalent natural phrasing is acceptable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What do we call a person who offers their time without payment?', 'A volunteer', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-070', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-retell-lecture', 'Re-tell Lecture', 'Repair cafes', 'Listen to the lecture. After 10 seconds of preparation, retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Repair cafes teach owners maintenance skills through participation, while records of failed repairs can suggest design issues but cannot establish their prevalence because visitors bring a self-selected sample of products.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A repair cafe brings volunteers and residents together to fix household objects. Its purpose is not simply to save the price of a replacement. By explaining each step, volunteers help owners understand why an object failed and how to maintain it. Some visitors arrive expecting a free repair service, however, and feel disappointed when they must participate. Organisers therefore describe the learning element clearly before accepting bookings. They also record items that cannot be repaired. These records can reveal recurring design problems, although they cannot establish how common a fault is across all products sold. A cafe sees only the objects that people choose to bring. Manufacturers could still use this limited evidence to identify components worth investigating. The strongest argument for a cafe is consequently educational rather than statistical: a successful visit can change the way someone thinks about ownership, even when the object itself remains broken.', 'Repair cafes teach owners maintenance skills through participation, while records of failed repairs can suggest design issues but cannot establish their prevalence because visitors bring a self-selected sample of products.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-071', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-describe-image', 'Describe Image', 'Fictional survey on repair cafes', 'Study the bar chart for 25 seconds. Describe its main features and comparisons in 40 seconds. Data are fictional.', 40, 25, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Identify the survey topic, compare the largest and smallest categories, and note that positive responses total 75%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The chart presents responses to a fictional survey about repair cafes. 45 percent considered it very useful and 30 percent somewhat useful. The two less positive categories accounted for 15 and 10 percent. Overall, positive responses made up 75 percent of the total.', 'data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20760%20380%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20fill%3D%22white%22%2F%3E%3Cg%20fill%3D%22%23172554%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2218%22%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2230%22%3EFictional%20survey%20on%20repair%20cafes%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2258%22%3EFictional%20survey%3A%20percentage%20of%20respondents%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22115%22%3EVery%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%2295%22%20width%3D%22180%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22410%22%20y%3D%22117%22%3E45%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22175%22%3ESomewhat%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22155%22%20width%3D%22120%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22350%22%20y%3D%22177%22%3E30%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22235%22%3ENot%20very%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22215%22%20width%3D%2260%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22290%22%20y%3D%22237%22%3E15%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22295%22%3ENot%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22275%22%20width%3D%2240%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22270%22%20y%3D%22297%22%3E10%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Very useful: 45%; Somewhat useful: 30%; Not very useful: 15%; Not useful: 10%'),
('pte-expansion-072', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'Night-time bus trials', 'Summarise the passage in ONE sentence of 5-75 words. You have 10 minutes.', 600, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Although a late bus trial attracted few passengers, interviews revealed employment benefits and limited publicity, leading researchers to recommend broader evaluation and comparison with alternatives before a final funding decision.', NULL, NULL, 'A city transport team tested a later bus service on two routes for six weeks. Passenger numbers were modest, so an initial report recommended cancellation. Interviews subsequently showed that several shift workers had accepted evening work because the buses gave them a reliable way home. Counting journeys alone had overlooked this benefit. The team also discovered that publicity had reached regular passengers but few potential new users. A longer trial with wider advertising might therefore produce different results. Nevertheless, the interviews did not prove that demand would eventually cover operating costs. The researchers recommended comparing the service with alternatives, including a shared taxi scheme. They proposed recording who benefited, how reliably vehicles arrived and the cost per completed journey. The council postponed its final decision until this broader evidence was available. Suppose a service carries a nurse who would otherwise be unable to work a late shift. Ticket revenue captures only part of that journey''s value. It would also be misleading to assume that every passenger experiences a benefit of this size. Evaluators need evidence about actual users and their available options. They should distinguish temporary lack of awareness from persistent lack of demand. Weather, shift patterns and the timing of a trial can affect use. A transparent report would present these uncertainties alongside costs, allowing elected representatives to decide which outcomes they value and what support they can provide.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Although a late bus trial attracted few passengers, interviews revealed employment benefits and limited publicity, leading researchers to recommend broader evaluation and comparison with alternatives before a final funding decision.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-073', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-read-aloud', 'Read Aloud', 'Night-time bus trials', 'Prepare for 35 seconds, then read the passage aloud clearly and naturally.', 40, 35, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Read all words accurately; group words into meaningful phrases rather than pausing after each word.', NULL, NULL, 'A city transport team tested a later bus service on two routes for six weeks. Passenger numbers were modest, so an initial report recommended cancellation. Interviews subsequently showed that several shift workers had accepted evening work because the buses gave them a reliable way home.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-074', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-repeat-sentence', 'Repeat Sentence', 'Night-time bus trials', 'Listen, then repeat the sentence exactly as spoken.', 15, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Preserve the original word sequence and grammatical endings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The last bus leaves the main entrance at midnight.', 'The last bus leaves the main entrance at midnight.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-075', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-answer-short-question', 'Answer Short Questions', 'Night-time bus trials', 'Listen to the question and answer with one or a few words.', 10, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Expected answer: A fare. Equivalent natural phrasing is acceptable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What is the usual name for the money a passenger pays for a bus journey?', 'A fare', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-076', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-retell-lecture', 'Re-tell Lecture', 'Night-time bus trials', 'Listen to the lecture. After 10 seconds of preparation, retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Although a late bus trial attracted few passengers, interviews revealed employment benefits and limited publicity, leading researchers to recommend broader evaluation and comparison with alternatives before a final funding decision.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A city transport team tested a later bus service on two routes for six weeks. Passenger numbers were modest, so an initial report recommended cancellation. Interviews subsequently showed that several shift workers had accepted evening work because the buses gave them a reliable way home. Counting journeys alone had overlooked this benefit. The team also discovered that publicity had reached regular passengers but few potential new users. A longer trial with wider advertising might therefore produce different results. Nevertheless, the interviews did not prove that demand would eventually cover operating costs. The researchers recommended comparing the service with alternatives, including a shared taxi scheme. They proposed recording who benefited, how reliably vehicles arrived and the cost per completed journey. The council postponed its final decision until this broader evidence was available.', 'Although a late bus trial attracted few passengers, interviews revealed employment benefits and limited publicity, leading researchers to recommend broader evaluation and comparison with alternatives before a final funding decision.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-077', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-describe-image', 'Describe Image', 'Fictional survey on night-time bus trials', 'Study the bar chart for 25 seconds. Describe its main features and comparisons in 40 seconds. Data are fictional.', 40, 25, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Identify the survey topic, compare the largest and smallest categories, and note that positive responses total 72%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The chart presents responses to a fictional survey about night-time bus trials. 38 percent considered it very useful and 34 percent somewhat useful. The two less positive categories accounted for 20 and 8 percent. Overall, positive responses made up 72 percent of the total.', 'data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20760%20380%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20fill%3D%22white%22%2F%3E%3Cg%20fill%3D%22%23172554%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2218%22%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2230%22%3EFictional%20survey%20on%20night-time%20bus%20trials%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2258%22%3EFictional%20survey%3A%20percentage%20of%20respondents%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22115%22%3EVery%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%2295%22%20width%3D%22152%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22382%22%20y%3D%22117%22%3E38%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22175%22%3ESomewhat%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22155%22%20width%3D%22136%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22366%22%20y%3D%22177%22%3E34%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22235%22%3ENot%20very%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22215%22%20width%3D%2280%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22310%22%20y%3D%22237%22%3E20%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22295%22%3ENot%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22275%22%20width%3D%2232%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22262%22%20y%3D%22297%22%3E8%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Very useful: 38%; Somewhat useful: 34%; Not very useful: 20%; Not useful: 8%'),
('pte-expansion-078', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'Museum object labels', 'Summarise the passage in ONE sentence of 5-75 words. You have 10 minutes.', 600, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'A museum combined question-based labels with optional detailed information after observing that accessible prompts encouraged family discussion, while recognising that longer visits alone did not demonstrate improved learning.', NULL, NULL, 'A regional museum replaced several technical labels with questions inviting visitors to examine the objects closely. One label beside a ceramic bowl asked what marks on its base might reveal about production. Visitors spent longer at the display, but the museum did not immediately conclude that they had learned more. Longer visits could indicate curiosity, confusion or simply congestion in a narrow gallery. Staff therefore observed conversations and invited visitors to explain one feature they had noticed. These additional measures suggested that the questions encouraged discussion between adults and children. Some specialists nevertheless preferred the detailed terminology on the original labels. The museum responded by keeping the introductory questions and adding optional information cards nearby. This layered approach offered different levels of detail without requiring everyone to read the same long text. The distinction between attention and understanding matters in many learning environments. A colourful display can hold attention without explaining a difficult idea. Conversely, a brief interaction may help someone notice a feature they would otherwise miss. A question about tool marks invited visitors to look back at the bowl rather than just read a description. Staff could then listen for explanations grounded in observation. This was more informative than recording time alone. The museum also considered readers with different language backgrounds, making the first layer clear while preserving precise terms for those who wanted them.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A museum combined question-based labels with optional detailed information after observing that accessible prompts encouraged family discussion, while recognising that longer visits alone did not demonstrate improved learning.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-079', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-read-aloud', 'Read Aloud', 'Museum object labels', 'Prepare for 35 seconds, then read the passage aloud clearly and naturally.', 40, 35, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Read all words accurately; group words into meaningful phrases rather than pausing after each word.', NULL, NULL, 'A regional museum replaced several technical labels with questions inviting visitors to examine the objects closely. One label beside a ceramic bowl asked what marks on its base might reveal about production. Visitors spent longer at the display, but the museum did not immediately conclude that they had learned more.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-080', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-repeat-sentence', 'Repeat Sentence', 'Museum object labels', 'Listen, then repeat the sentence exactly as spoken.', 15, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Preserve the original word sequence and grammatical endings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Detailed information cards are available beside the exhibition entrance.', 'Detailed information cards are available beside the exhibition entrance.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-081', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-answer-short-question', 'Answer Short Questions', 'Museum object labels', 'Listen to the question and answer with one or a few words.', 10, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Expected answer: A visitor. Equivalent natural phrasing is acceptable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What do we call a person who visits a museum?', 'A visitor', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-082', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-retell-lecture', 'Re-tell Lecture', 'Museum object labels', 'Listen to the lecture. After 10 seconds of preparation, retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'A museum combined question-based labels with optional detailed information after observing that accessible prompts encouraged family discussion, while recognising that longer visits alone did not demonstrate improved learning.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A regional museum replaced several technical labels with questions inviting visitors to examine the objects closely. One label beside a ceramic bowl asked what marks on its base might reveal about production. Visitors spent longer at the display, but the museum did not immediately conclude that they had learned more. Longer visits could indicate curiosity, confusion or simply congestion in a narrow gallery. Staff therefore observed conversations and invited visitors to explain one feature they had noticed. These additional measures suggested that the questions encouraged discussion between adults and children. Some specialists nevertheless preferred the detailed terminology on the original labels. The museum responded by keeping the introductory questions and adding optional information cards nearby. This layered approach offered different levels of detail without requiring everyone to read the same long text.', 'A museum combined question-based labels with optional detailed information after observing that accessible prompts encouraged family discussion, while recognising that longer visits alone did not demonstrate improved learning.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-083', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-describe-image', 'Describe Image', 'Fictional survey on museum object labels', 'Study the bar chart for 25 seconds. Describe its main features and comparisons in 40 seconds. Data are fictional.', 40, 25, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Identify the survey topic, compare the largest and smallest categories, and note that positive responses total 80%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The chart presents responses to a fictional survey about museum object labels. 52 percent considered it very useful and 28 percent somewhat useful. The two less positive categories accounted for 12 and 8 percent. Overall, positive responses made up 80 percent of the total.', 'data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20760%20380%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20fill%3D%22white%22%2F%3E%3Cg%20fill%3D%22%23172554%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2218%22%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2230%22%3EFictional%20survey%20on%20museum%20object%20labels%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2258%22%3EFictional%20survey%3A%20percentage%20of%20respondents%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22115%22%3EVery%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%2295%22%20width%3D%22208%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22438%22%20y%3D%22117%22%3E52%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22175%22%3ESomewhat%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22155%22%20width%3D%22112%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22342%22%20y%3D%22177%22%3E28%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22235%22%3ENot%20very%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22215%22%20width%3D%2248%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22278%22%20y%3D%22237%22%3E12%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22295%22%3ENot%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22275%22%20width%3D%2232%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22262%22%20y%3D%22297%22%3E8%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Very useful: 52%; Somewhat useful: 28%; Not very useful: 12%; Not useful: 8%'),
('pte-expansion-084', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'Shared research equipment', 'Summarise the passage in ONE sentence of 5-75 words. You have 10 minutes.', 600, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Departments sharing an imaging instrument found that protected maintenance and coordinated scheduling improved reliability despite slightly lower utilisation, demonstrating that successful sharing involves more than reducing purchase costs.', NULL, NULL, 'Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user. A committee initially proposed charging departments for every minute of access. Technicians warned that this might discourage necessary cleaning and calibration between sessions. The committee instead introduced protected maintenance periods and required users to estimate preparation time separately from measurement time. It also appointed a coordinator to resolve conflicts. Utilisation fell slightly because the timetable now included maintenance, yet fewer experiments had to be repeated. The departments concluded that keeping the machine continuously occupied was a poor substitute for producing reliable results. Sharing equipment required investment in coordination as well as agreement over purchase costs. A utilisation figure can look impressive while concealing avoidable errors. If a machine runs all day but produces measurements that must be repeated, the apparent efficiency is misleading. Maintenance may reduce available booking hours while increasing useful output. The coordinator therefore tracked repeat experiments and reasons for delays alongside total use. Researchers also received training in estimating their needs. This did not remove every conflict, especially before important deadlines, but it made the basis for allocating time clearer. Departments considering shared facilities could begin by discussing these practical responsibilities rather than focusing exclusively on the price of the instrument.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Departments sharing an imaging instrument found that protected maintenance and coordinated scheduling improved reliability despite slightly lower utilisation, demonstrating that successful sharing involves more than reducing purchase costs.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-085', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-read-aloud', 'Read Aloud', 'Shared research equipment', 'Prepare for 35 seconds, then read the passage aloud clearly and naturally.', 40, 35, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Read all words accurately; group words into meaningful phrases rather than pausing after each word.', NULL, NULL, 'Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-086', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-repeat-sentence', 'Repeat Sentence', 'Shared research equipment', 'Listen, then repeat the sentence exactly as spoken.', 15, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Preserve the original word sequence and grammatical endings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Please include preparation time when booking the shared equipment.', 'Please include preparation time when booking the shared equipment.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-087', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-answer-short-question', 'Answer Short Questions', 'Shared research equipment', 'Listen to the question and answer with one or a few words.', 10, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Expected answer: A thermometer. Equivalent natural phrasing is acceptable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What instrument is commonly used to measure temperature?', 'A thermometer', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-088', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-retell-lecture', 'Re-tell Lecture', 'Shared research equipment', 'Listen to the lecture. After 10 seconds of preparation, retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Departments sharing an imaging instrument found that protected maintenance and coordinated scheduling improved reliability despite slightly lower utilisation, demonstrating that successful sharing involves more than reducing purchase costs.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Several university departments agreed to share an expensive imaging instrument instead of buying separate machines. The arrangement reduced initial expenditure, but scheduling soon became difficult. Experiments needed different amounts of preparation, and a short booking sometimes delayed the following user. A committee initially proposed charging departments for every minute of access. Technicians warned that this might discourage necessary cleaning and calibration between sessions. The committee instead introduced protected maintenance periods and required users to estimate preparation time separately from measurement time. It also appointed a coordinator to resolve conflicts. Utilisation fell slightly because the timetable now included maintenance, yet fewer experiments had to be repeated. The departments concluded that keeping the machine continuously occupied was a poor substitute for producing reliable results. Sharing equipment required investment in coordination as well as agreement over purchase costs.', 'Departments sharing an imaging instrument found that protected maintenance and coordinated scheduling improved reliability despite slightly lower utilisation, demonstrating that successful sharing involves more than reducing purchase costs.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-089', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-describe-image', 'Describe Image', 'Fictional survey on shared research equipment', 'Study the bar chart for 25 seconds. Describe its main features and comparisons in 40 seconds. Data are fictional.', 40, 25, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Identify the survey topic, compare the largest and smallest categories, and note that positive responses total 76%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The chart presents responses to a fictional survey about shared research equipment. 41 percent considered it very useful and 35 percent somewhat useful. The two less positive categories accounted for 18 and 6 percent. Overall, positive responses made up 76 percent of the total.', 'data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20760%20380%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20fill%3D%22white%22%2F%3E%3Cg%20fill%3D%22%23172554%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2218%22%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2230%22%3EFictional%20survey%20on%20shared%20research%20equipment%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2258%22%3EFictional%20survey%3A%20percentage%20of%20respondents%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22115%22%3EVery%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%2295%22%20width%3D%22164%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22394%22%20y%3D%22117%22%3E41%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22175%22%3ESomewhat%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22155%22%20width%3D%22140%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22370%22%20y%3D%22177%22%3E35%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22235%22%3ENot%20very%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22215%22%20width%3D%2272%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22302%22%20y%3D%22237%22%3E18%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22295%22%3ENot%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22275%22%20width%3D%2224%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22254%22%20y%3D%22297%22%3E6%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Very useful: 41%; Somewhat useful: 35%; Not very useful: 18%; Not useful: 6%'),
('pte-expansion-090', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'summarize-written-text', 'Summarize Written Text', 'Community rainfall records', 'Summarise the passage in ONE sentence of 5-75 words. You have 10 minutes.', 600, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated. Imagine two neighbouring diaries showing different totals for the same month. One observer may have measured in an open space, while another kept a container beneath a tree. Without contextual notes, a researcher might interpret the difference as a variation in weather. Documentation does not tell us exactly how much rain fell, but it helps us avoid unjustified certainty. The distinction between missing and zero values is equally important. A person may have been away for a week or simply forgotten to write. Preserving that uncertainty is more honest than filling every empty cell with a convenient number.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-091', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-read-aloud', 'Read Aloud', 'Community rainfall records', 'Prepare for 35 seconds, then read the passage aloud clearly and naturally.', 40, 35, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Read all words accurately; group words into meaningful phrases rather than pausing after each word.', NULL, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-092', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-repeat-sentence', 'Repeat Sentence', 'Community rainfall records', 'Listen, then repeat the sentence exactly as spoken.', 15, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Preserve the original word sequence and grammatical endings.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The original diaries remain available in the local history archive.', 'The original diaries remain available in the local history archive.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-093', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-answer-short-question', 'Answer Short Questions', 'Community rainfall records', 'Listen to the question and answer with one or a few words.', 10, 0, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Expected answer: Rain. Equivalent natural phrasing is acceptable.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'What do we call water that falls from clouds in liquid drops?', 'Rain', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-094', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-retell-lecture', 'Re-tell Lecture', 'Community rainfall records', 'Listen to the lecture. After 10 seconds of preparation, retell the main points in your own words in 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'A local history group digitised handwritten rainfall diaries kept by residents over many decades. The records offered information from places where official weather stations had never operated. However, the volunteers noticed that observers had used different containers and sometimes moved them between gardens. These changes could affect the amounts recorded. Rather than discarding the diaries, the group attached notes describing known changes in method and location. Researchers could then decide which comparisons were defensible. A missing entry was left blank rather than treated as a day without rain. The project also retained images of the original pages so that uncertain handwriting could be checked. Its value lay not in producing a perfectly uniform series, but in making a varied historical record available with its limitations visible. Careful documentation allowed later users to ask questions that the original observers had never anticipated.', 'Volunteers made historical rainfall diaries useful for research by digitising them while documenting inconsistent methods, retaining original images and distinguishing missing observations from dry days.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-095', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-describe-image', 'Describe Image', 'Fictional survey on community rainfall records', 'Study the bar chart for 25 seconds. Describe its main features and comparisons in 40 seconds. Data are fictional.', 40, 25, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Identify the survey topic, compare the largest and smallest categories, and note that positive responses total 76%.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'The chart presents responses to a fictional survey about community rainfall records. 36 percent considered it very useful and 40 percent somewhat useful. The two less positive categories accounted for 16 and 8 percent. Overall, positive responses made up 76 percent of the total.', 'data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20760%20380%22%3E%3Crect%20width%3D%22760%22%20height%3D%22380%22%20fill%3D%22white%22%2F%3E%3Cg%20fill%3D%22%23172554%22%20font-family%3D%22Arial%22%20font-size%3D%2218%22%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2230%22%3EFictional%20survey%20on%20community%20rainfall%20records%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%2258%22%3EFictional%20survey%3A%20percentage%20of%20respondents%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22115%22%3EVery%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%2295%22%20width%3D%22144%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22374%22%20y%3D%22117%22%3E36%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22175%22%3ESomewhat%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22155%22%20width%3D%22160%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22390%22%20y%3D%22177%22%3E40%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22235%22%3ENot%20very%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22215%22%20width%3D%2264%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22294%22%20y%3D%22237%22%3E16%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%2220%22%20y%3D%22295%22%3ENot%20useful%3C%2Ftext%3E%3Crect%20x%3D%22220%22%20y%3D%22275%22%20width%3D%2232%22%20height%3D%2230%22%20fill%3D%22%232563eb%22%2F%3E%3Ctext%20x%3D%22262%22%20y%3D%22297%22%3E8%25%3C%2Ftext%3E%3C%2Fg%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E', 'Very useful: 36%; Somewhat useful: 40%; Not very useful: 16%; Not useful: 8%'),
('pte-expansion-096', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-write-essay', 'Write Essay', 'Assessment design', 'Universities should use practical projects rather than final examinations as the main form of assessment. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Compare authentic application with consistency of marking; consider individual accountability in group projects. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-097', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-write-essay', 'Write Essay', 'Local journalism', 'Public funding should support local journalism in communities where commercial news services have closed. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Consider civic information, editorial independence, transparent funding and alternatives to subsidy. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-098', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-write-essay', 'Write Essay', 'Product lifespan', 'Manufacturers should be required to publish the expected useful life of household appliances. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Discuss informed purchasing, measurement uncertainty, repairability and enforcement. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-099', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-write-essay', 'Write Essay', 'Workplace mentoring', 'Employers should allocate paid working time for experienced staff to mentor new colleagues. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Consider training quality, mentor workload, retention and how the programme could be evaluated. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-100', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-write-essay', 'Write Essay', 'Public space', 'Cities should give priority to pedestrian access rather than private vehicle parking in central shopping areas. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Balance safety and public space with disability access, deliveries and business concerns. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-101', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-repeated-essay-questions', 'Repeated Essay Questions', 'Digital archives', 'Museums should prioritise making collections available online over expanding their physical buildings. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes. This is an original practice prompt, not a recalled exam question.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Compare geographic access with preservation costs and the value of viewing objects in person. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-102', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-repeated-essay-questions', 'Repeated Essay Questions', 'Flexible education', 'Adult learners should be able to complete university qualifications through short modules taken over several years. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes. This is an original practice prompt, not a recalled exam question.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Discuss access, continuity, academic standards and recognition of accumulated learning. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-103', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-repeated-essay-questions', 'Repeated Essay Questions', 'Food waste reporting', 'Large food retailers should be required to publish annual reports on the food they discard. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes. This is an original practice prompt, not a recalled exam question.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Consider accountability, comparable definitions, reporting costs and whether disclosure changes behaviour. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-104', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-repeated-essay-questions', 'Repeated Essay Questions', 'Transport trials', 'Governments should test major transport changes through temporary trials before making them permanent. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes. This is an original practice prompt, not a recalled exam question.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Discuss evidence gathering, disruption, trial duration and the risk of unrepresentative results. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-105', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'writing', 'pte-repeated-essay-questions', 'Repeated Essay Questions', 'Community expertise', 'Local residents should have a formal role in designing university research about their communities. To what extent do you agree or disagree? Support your view with reasons and examples. Write 200-300 words in 20 minutes. This is an original practice prompt, not a recalled exam question.', 1200, 0, 0, 15, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Consider relevance, representation, research independence and practical collaboration. State and sustain a clear position. There is no preferred opinion.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-106', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-summarise-group-discussion', 'Summarise Group Discussion', 'Study room booking', 'Listen to three students discussing a proposal. After 10 seconds of preparation, summarise their views and how the discussion develops. Speak for up to 2 minutes. This is a shortened synthetic-voice practice discussion, not an exam recording.', 120, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Include the initial proposal, Blair''s concern, Casey''s compromise and the agreed next step. Attribute views accurately rather than listing disconnected keywords.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Alex: We should allow students to book the quiet room for two hours. During exams, people need enough time to complete a serious piece of work. Blair: Two hours may keep everyone else waiting. I would prefer shorter bookings, especially because some students book rooms and never arrive. Casey: We can keep the two-hour limit but release a booking after fifteen minutes if nobody checks in. That tackles unused reservations without interrupting genuine study. Blair: I could support that, provided students get a reminder and can cancel easily. Alex: Let us trial check-in reminders and the release rule for two weeks, then compare waiting times and complaints.', 'Alex proposes: We should allow students to book the quiet room for two hours. During exams, people need enough time to complete a serious piece of work. Blair raises a concern: Two hours may keep everyone else waiting. I would prefer shorter bookings, especially because some students book rooms and never arrive. Casey suggests a compromise: We can keep the two-hour limit but release a booking after fifteen minutes if nobody checks in. That tackles unused reservations without interrupting genuine study. The agreed next step is: Let us trial check-in reminders and the release rule for two weeks, then compare waiting times and complaints.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-107', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-summarise-group-discussion', 'Summarise Group Discussion', 'Campus garden', 'Listen to three students discussing a proposal. After 10 seconds of preparation, summarise their views and how the discussion develops. Speak for up to 2 minutes. This is a shortened synthetic-voice practice discussion, not an exam recording.', 120, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Include the initial proposal, Blair''s concern, Casey''s compromise and the agreed next step. Attribute views accurately rather than listing disconnected keywords.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Alex: The unused courtyard could become a vegetable garden. Students would gain practical experience and we could donate some produce. Blair: Who would water it during holidays? A garden that depends entirely on students might be neglected when everyone leaves. Casey: We could begin with a few beds and ask the grounds team about holiday cover before expanding. Starting small would reveal the workload. Blair: That is more realistic than planting the whole courtyard immediately. We should also check access to water. Alex: I will ask the grounds team about water and maintenance, and we can develop a small pilot if support is available.', 'Alex proposes: The unused courtyard could become a vegetable garden. Students would gain practical experience and we could donate some produce. Blair raises a concern: Who would water it during holidays? A garden that depends entirely on students might be neglected when everyone leaves. Casey suggests a compromise: We could begin with a few beds and ask the grounds team about holiday cover before expanding. Starting small would reveal the workload. The agreed next step is: I will ask the grounds team about water and maintenance, and we can develop a small pilot if support is available.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-108', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-summarise-group-discussion', 'Summarise Group Discussion', 'Recorded lectures', 'Listen to three students discussing a proposal. After 10 seconds of preparation, summarise their views and how the discussion develops. Speak for up to 2 minutes. This is a shortened synthetic-voice practice discussion, not an exam recording.', 120, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Include the initial proposal, Blair''s concern, Casey''s compromise and the agreed next step. Attribute views accurately rather than listing disconnected keywords.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Alex: We should ask lecturers to record every session. Students with caring responsibilities sometimes miss classes and need another way to follow the course. Blair: Recordings help, but students may stop attending. Some discussions also include personal examples that people would not want shared. Casey: What about recording the presentation but pausing during sensitive discussion? We could keep activities in class that are worth attending for. Blair: I like separating the presentation from discussion. Clear access rules would also reassure people. Alex: Let us propose recordings of presentation segments, restricted to the class, and ask students and lecturers to review the arrangement after a month.', 'Alex proposes: We should ask lecturers to record every session. Students with caring responsibilities sometimes miss classes and need another way to follow the course. Blair raises a concern: Recordings help, but students may stop attending. Some discussions also include personal examples that people would not want shared. Casey suggests a compromise: What about recording the presentation but pausing during sensitive discussion? We could keep activities in class that are worth attending for. The agreed next step is: Let us propose recordings of presentation segments, restricted to the class, and ask students and lecturers to review the arrangement after a month.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-109', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-summarise-group-discussion', 'Summarise Group Discussion', 'Volunteer induction', 'Listen to three students discussing a proposal. After 10 seconds of preparation, summarise their views and how the discussion develops. Speak for up to 2 minutes. This is a shortened synthetic-voice practice discussion, not an exam recording.', 120, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Include the initial proposal, Blair''s concern, Casey''s compromise and the agreed next step. Attribute views accurately rather than listing disconnected keywords.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Alex: Our volunteer programme needs a longer induction. New members say they arrive without knowing whom to ask for help. Blair: A whole extra training day could deter people who already have limited time. We need to make joining easier, not harder. Casey: We could send a short guide before the first session and assign each newcomer a named buddy. Practical questions could then be answered during the work. Blair: A buddy would be useful, especially if the guide explains the basic safety rules clearly. Alex: Let us try the guide and buddy system with the next intake, then ask whether newcomers felt prepared and supported.', 'Alex proposes: Our volunteer programme needs a longer induction. New members say they arrive without knowing whom to ask for help. Blair raises a concern: A whole extra training day could deter people who already have limited time. We need to make joining easier, not harder. Casey suggests a compromise: We could send a short guide before the first session and assign each newcomer a named buddy. Practical questions could then be answered during the work. The agreed next step is: Let us try the guide and buddy system with the next intake, then ask whether newcomers felt prepared and supported.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-110', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-summarise-group-discussion', 'Summarise Group Discussion', 'Student newsletter', 'Listen to three students discussing a proposal. After 10 seconds of preparation, summarise their views and how the discussion develops. Speak for up to 2 minutes. This is a shortened synthetic-voice practice discussion, not an exam recording.', 120, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Include the initial proposal, Blair''s concern, Casey''s compromise and the agreed next step. Attribute views accurately rather than listing disconnected keywords.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Alex: The student newsletter should become digital only. Printing costs are rising, and online articles could be updated when event details change. Blair: Some students prefer a paper copy, and an email can be easy to overlook. Removing print entirely might reduce the audience. Casey: Could we publish the full version online and print a one-page events sheet for noticeboards? That would preserve a visible reminder without printing every article. Blair: Yes, and the sheet could include a short address for the full version. We should not rely only on codes people must scan. Alex: We can compare readership and costs for one term using a digital edition and a brief printed events sheet.', 'Alex proposes: The student newsletter should become digital only. Printing costs are rising, and online articles could be updated when event details change. Blair raises a concern: Some students prefer a paper copy, and an email can be easy to overlook. Removing print entirely might reduce the audience. Casey suggests a compromise: Could we publish the full version online and print a one-page events sheet for noticeboards? That would preserve a visible reminder without printing every article. The agreed next step is: We can compare readership and costs for one term using a digital edition and a brief printed events sheet.', NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-111', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-respond-to-situation', 'Respond to a Situation', 'Overlapping deadlines', 'You have two assignments due on Friday and your tutor has offered a meeting on Thursday. You need advice before you can finish one assignment. Call the tutor, explain the conflict and politely ask whether an earlier meeting is possible. Prepare for 10 seconds, then respond directly to the person for up to 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Explain the deadline, request an earlier appointment and offer flexibility without demanding an extension.', NULL, NULL, 'You have two assignments due on Friday and your tutor has offered a meeting on Thursday. You need advice before you can finish one assignment. Call the tutor, explain the conflict and politely ask whether an earlier meeting is possible.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'You have two assignments due on Friday and your tutor has offered a meeting on Thursday. You need advice before you can finish one assignment. Call the tutor, explain the conflict and politely ask whether an earlier meeting is possible.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-112', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-respond-to-situation', 'Respond to a Situation', 'Incorrect delivery', 'You ordered ten folders for a student event tomorrow, but only six arrived. Speak to the supplier, explain what is missing and ask for a practical solution before the event. Prepare for 10 seconds, then respond directly to the person for up to 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'State the quantity ordered and received, mention tomorrow''s event and request delivery of the remaining four or an alternative.', NULL, NULL, 'You ordered ten folders for a student event tomorrow, but only six arrived. Speak to the supplier, explain what is missing and ask for a practical solution before the event.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'You ordered ten folders for a student event tomorrow, but only six arrived. Speak to the supplier, explain what is missing and ask for a practical solution before the event.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-113', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-respond-to-situation', 'Respond to a Situation', 'Shared kitchen', 'Your flatmate often leaves dishes in the shared sink overnight, making it difficult for you to prepare breakfast. Speak to your flatmate politely, describe the problem and suggest an arrangement. Prepare for 10 seconds, then respond directly to the person for up to 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Use a respectful tone, explain the practical effect and propose an agreed cleaning routine.', NULL, NULL, 'Your flatmate often leaves dishes in the shared sink overnight, making it difficult for you to prepare breakfast. Speak to your flatmate politely, describe the problem and suggest an arrangement.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Your flatmate often leaves dishes in the shared sink overnight, making it difficult for you to prepare breakfast. Speak to your flatmate politely, describe the problem and suggest an arrangement.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-114', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-respond-to-situation', 'Respond to a Situation', 'Room change', 'You organise a study group of eight people. The library has moved your booking to a room with only four chairs. Speak to the librarian and ask for a suitable arrangement without disturbing other users. Prepare for 10 seconds, then respond directly to the person for up to 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Explain the booking size, identify the seating problem and ask about another room or additional seating.', NULL, NULL, 'You organise a study group of eight people. The library has moved your booking to a room with only four chairs. Speak to the librarian and ask for a suitable arrangement without disturbing other users.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'You organise a study group of eight people. The library has moved your booking to a room with only four chairs. Speak to the librarian and ask for a suitable arrangement without disturbing other users.', NULL, NULL, NULL),
('pte-expansion-115', 'pte-2026-01', 'PTE', ARRAY['PTE'], 'speaking', 'pte-respond-to-situation', 'Respond to a Situation', 'Missed shift', 'Your train has been cancelled and you will arrive thirty minutes late for your volunteer shift. Phone the coordinator, explain the delay and ask how you can minimise the disruption. Prepare for 10 seconds, then respond directly to the person for up to 40 seconds.', 40, 10, 0, 10, 'medium', ARRAY['PTE','Original practice','Expansion 2026'], 'Give timely notice, apologise, estimate arrival and offer a practical way to help rather than making excuses.', NULL, NULL, 'Your train has been cancelled and you will arrive thirty minutes late for your volunteer shift. Phone the coordinator, explain the delay and ask how you can minimise the disruption.', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Your train has been cancelled and you will arrive thirty minutes late for your volunteer shift. Phone the coordinator, explain the delay and ask how you can minimise the disruption.', NULL, NULL, NULL)
